      "content": "i guess but \"embracing the struggle\" sounds like a way to just prolong the inevitable. if existence is inherently indifferent and we're just reacting to stimuli in a void, why is it considered \"correct\" to keep pushing through it? it feels like we're just being told to keep running on a treadmill that's going nowhere. isn't there a certain logic to just... stopping? to accepting the void instead of fighting a battle that's rigged from the start?",
